0..45 Comment "// Vectors are lists indexed by their length."
46..48 Comment "//"
49..125 Comment "// A vector\'s type states its length. A function then states the length that"
126..140 Comment "// it returns."
141..143 Comment "//"
144..219 Comment "// The kind `Nat -> Type` reads the type of the length before the universe."
220..298 Comment "// `VNil` stands at zero. `VCons` stands at one past the length of its tail. A"
299..376 Comment "// length written as a call stands at the length that the call computes. Thus"
377..456 Comment "// `plus(m, Zero)` is the length `m`. The pathological twin holds the refusals."
457..459 Comment "//"
460..538 Comment "// - see: Dybjer, _Inductive families_, FAC 1994, doi:10.1007/BF01211308 — a"
539..604 Comment "//   family whose constructors each state the index they stand at"
605..686 Comment "// - see: #3579 — a family\'s argument written as a call converts with its value"
687..764 Comment "// - see: #3625 — a constructor\'s field written as a call meets a type that"
765..785 Comment "//   writes the call"
786..863 Comment "// - see: #3627 — a constructor at a length written as a call that computes"
864..889 Comment "//   the length it states"
891..928 Comment "// The naturals the lengths count in."
929..935 Keyword "import"
936..937 StringLit "\""
